{
  "assembly_notes": "Single source (SOURCES=1). The fold-out conversion mechanism is a fixed shared core: one rigid sofa_frame root, one fixed seat_deck middle bed panel, a REVOLUTE backrest that reclines flat rearward onto fixed rear support legs, a REVOLUTE foot_panel that folds out forward to bed height, and deck_leg_count REVOLUTE fold-down deck legs under the foot panel (each with a real captured pivot receiver). Three peripheral component slots vary by controlled world-knowledge extrapolation without touching the mechanism: base_leg (4 rigid corner legs), arm_style (2 rigid arms), deck_support (fold-down deck-leg station geometry). deck_leg_count is a structural multiplicity on deck_support. width_m, seat_depth_m, and bed_height_m are independent continuous parameters that derive frame/seat/backrest/foot geometry, hinge positions, arm span, leg positions, and deck-leg length; palette and tufting are non-core.",
